            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>BIII-890-CL is a non-orally active sodium channel blocker under development by Boehringer Ingelheim Corp for the potential treatment of thromboembolic stroke. By April 2001, the compound was in phase II clinical trials for this indication, with trials ongoing in June 2002. The compound is also under investigation for its potential use in the treatment of pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
